Package: pubsubr
Type: Package
Title: Serverless Publish-Subscribe Interprocess Messaging
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("formix", email = "formix@users.noreply.github.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A serverless publish-subscribe library for local interprocess
    communication. Messages are routed through kernel FIFO named pipes and
    stored on the shared-memory filesystem ('/dev/shm' on Linux), with no
    broker or server process. This is a literal translation of the Python
    'formix-pubsub' library and uses the same on-disk and wire formats, so R
    and Python processes can exchange messages. Requires R >= 3.5.0 for
    suspendInterrupts(), so that an interrupt (SIGINT, caught as an
    'interrupt' condition) never stops a message half-processed. SIGTERM
    is handled when the optional 'sigterm' package
    (<https://github.com/atheriel/sigterm>) is installed.
